{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-categorical-neutron-unique","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proof","doco:Section"],"label":"prf:categorical-neutron-unique","kind":"proof","title":"Proof of uniqueness of the categorical neutron","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-neutron-unique"],"text":"categorical-neutron-unique-proof.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prf:categorical-neutron-unique\"></a><p>The argument is identical to that for the <a href=\"#prop:categorical-proton-unique\" data-at=\"predicted-spectra/mesons-nucleons-categorical-proton-unique\">uniqueness of the categorical proton</a>, applying the partition <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathfrak{u}, \\mathfrak{d}, \\mathfrak{d})</code>. The Hecke normal form in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_3(q)</code> is unique. The <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">S_3</code>-colour symmetry relates the three position assignments via inner automorphisms. Furthermore, the LP-optimal two-gluon stabiliser uniquely minimizes <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">|\\mathrm{tr}_M|</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/categorical-neutron-unique-proof.md","heading":"Proof","page":"b/prf-categorical-neutron-unique","qa":{"counts":{"pass":56,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":17,"unknown":0,"stale":58},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}}}
